[S3] Comment by Eswarar Siva (2026-10-28)
We ran into this on 4.3.2 and reproduced it, in case the details help with the priority.

Setup: processing.guarantee exactly_once_v2, one persistent (RocksDB, timestamped) global store, and a state.dir that is kept across restarts (a Kubernetes StatefulSet with a volume).

What we see: once the global store has flushed a memtable after it was opened, the "open" status in its offsets column family is on disk. A SIGKILL from then on (an OOM kill, or a kill after the shutdown grace period) leaves that status at 1, and every later start fails with TaskCorruptedException: "Tasks \[1-1\] are corrupted ... State store ... didn't find a valid state, since under EOS ... Invalid state during store open". The global thread dies and the "Detected unclean shutdown for global store" wipe in GlobalStateManagerImpl#initialize never runs, as described above. With at_least_once the same kill restarts fine, and so does a kill after a clean restart before the store's first flush. So for an exactly_once_v2 application with a persistent global store, a hard kill after that first flush ends in a crash loop until the global folder is deleted by hand.

As far as I can tell this came in with 4.3.0 (4.2 has no status key), and 4.3.2 and 4.4.0 both have it, so maybe those could go in as affected versions. A backport of the fix to 4.3.x and 4.4.x would help us a lot, if that is possible.

Happy to share the small reproduction if it is useful.
[S4] Comment by Eswarar Siva (2026-10-28)
I set the type to Bug and the priority to Major, since the existing wipe from KAFKA-17411 can no longer be reached after KAFKA-20396, which leaves a crash loop; also added the affected versions. Please change them back if you would triage it differently.
[S5] Comment by 이선민 (2026-10-29)
[~zoro30102000] Thanks for the detailed report. This matches the failure path addressed by my PR: under EOS, RocksDBStore#openDB wraps the invalid-state failure in TaskCorruptedException, which is not caught by the ProcessorStateException handler in GlobalStateManagerImpl#initialize, so the existing wipe is skipped for this path.

My open PR, https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/23390, handles this in GlobalStreamThread#initialize alongside InvalidOffsetException, closing the state consumer with wipeStateStore=true so the global store can be rebuilt on the next start. Review is ongoing, with discussion about where the cleanup should live and whether the existing cleanup paths should be unified.


Please share the reproduction; I'd like to validate the PR against it. If you're able to test the patch in your setup as well, that would be helpful. I'll also raise the request for backports to 4.3.x and 4.4.x with the committers.
